Let G be a locally compact group with left Haar measure, and let L^1(G) denote its group algebra, equipped with convolution as multiplication. Recall that a multi-norm on a normed space (E, ||·||) is a sequence (||·||_n) of norms on the products E^n (for n ∈ ℕ) satisfying the following axioms for all n and all (x_1, ..., x_n) ∈ E^n:
(M1) ||(x_σ(1), ..., x_σ(n))||_n = ||(x_1, ..., x_n)||_n for every permutation σ of {1, ..., n};
(M2) ||(α_1 x_1, ..., α_n x_n)||_n ≤ (max_i |α_i|) · ||(x_1, ..., x_n)||_n for all scalars α_i;
(M3) ||(x_1, ..., x_n, 0)||_{n+1} = ||(x_1, ..., x_n)||_n;
(M4) ||(x_1, ..., x_n, x_n)||_{n+1} = ||(x_1, ..., x_n)||_n;
and ||x||_1 = ||x|| for x ∈ E. A multi-Banach algebra is a Banach algebra (A, ||·||) together with a multi-norm (||·||_n) on A such that for each n,
   ||(a·b_1, ..., a·b_n)||_n ≤ ||a|| · ||(b_1, ..., b_n)||_n,
   ||(b_1·a, ..., b_n·a)||_n ≤ ||a|| · ||(b_1, ..., b_n)||_n,
for all a, b_1, ..., b_n ∈ A.

Characterize those multi-norms (||·||_n) on L^1(G) which make L^1(G) into a multi-Banach algebra, and determine what structural information about L^1(G) (and hence about G) can be extracted from such multi-norms.

